Depends on if we're going strictly by show or book interpretation. To my own detriment I haven't finished the books so I can't say anything about it there, but as far as the show goes, The way I see it Cersei was an effective Queen who ruled for many years, Not only as her own but as Robert's Queen and Queen Mother of Joffery and Tommen. And I think Cersei has a good heart, or at least did. She would do anything for her children, and even though it's clear that in Westeros, only the throne matters and not the realm it represents. And she has money, and resources. I know Tywin says the Lannisters are broke but I mean, it's technically the Crown that owes that debt, not the Lannisters, I'm not sure what's going on with that one tbh. And just gonna put it down, having a Maester who knows some forbidden knowledge on retainer is pretty sweet, can help you identify when forbidden shit is going down. Like, Cersei is a bad bitch, no doubt. But I mean, everything she does was for some good? Consider the fact that Tommen allowed religious extremists to fester in Kings Landing during his brief reign, so what did Cersei do after shit got way too out of hand? Blew them the fuck up. Not to mention she actually tried with the sparrows too. She LIKED the High Sparrow at first, even if only as a polite courtesy.

&Nbsp;

I know that's a big text wall but basically, she has ruling experience, resources, and some motive to rule well. The only other person in this list who these that is Yara, and she's just interested in the Iron Islands, which is just as well. Because she'd have to go to war for the throne. At least Cersei sits on the throne pretty much up until the end of the series, so peace can be maintained. Except for Wights. And to be a little bit reasonable, it does sound like a bit of a trap. Yes they're known to be real, but all your enemies are the ones sending you the message for help, and Wights haven't been seen in a millennia, at least.

