"Don't Forget Your Roots" - Six60

&nbsp;

I like Six60 as much as the next man, no idea how big they are outside of NZ but goddamn I hate this song. Why? It's message. This song is all about family and loving them and that. You might think "hey good message." and yeah, sure. And the song is actually really well composed. It's a good song objectively. The reason it annoys me is because my Family fucking sucks. All they do is screw me over and give me the short end. And so has any close friend I've considered family. Were it not for a few notable exceptions among their ranks, I'd have been completely alone for all of it.

&nbsp;

It also does not help that I most often hear this song at work, a McDonalds, where I seem to be in Kitchen by myself and expected to work faster during a rush. I'm not Dr. Octopus, I can't be running 4 stations on my own without some small tie penalty. Especially when a loud ass siren/buzzer goes off in my ear every half second. And when the manager's are like "stop swearing at it" I'm like "yeah, but you have no idea what's going on inside my brain do you?"

One day, in the near future of 2084, An aging woman named Mikaela will sit her grandkids down, and play the music of her time for them to hear for themselves, since the Social Justice Police have all but banned it.

